# fleet-dispatch.schedule -- WHEN each CI box dispatches which workflow (OPS-23).
#
# The single source of truth for the dispatch timers. Two readers:
#   - ops/install-fleet-dispatch.sh renders each `timer` line of the box's slot into
#     /etc/systemd/system/fleet-dispatch@<name>.timer.d/10-slot.conf as
#     OnCalendar=*-*-* *:<minutes>:00
#   - ops/dispatch_liveness.py (runner-health.yml, check-scheduler job) computes from
#     the same lines when each slot SHOULD have dispatched, and warns when it didn't.
#
# The two slots interleave, so both boxes together give the target cadence and either
# box alone still gives half of it:
#   runner-health.yml   every 30 min combined (a :00, b :30)          -> 60 min alone
#   queue-watchdog.yml  every 10 min combined (a :00/20/40, b :10/30/50) -> 20 min alone
#
# Format:
#   slot  <a|b>  <inventory host id>           which box carries that slot
#   timer <workflow file> <slot> <minutes>     minutes = MM or MM/step (systemd minute
#                                              field; times are UTC on the boxes)
# The workflow file is also the allowlist in ops/fleet-dispatch.sh; keep them in step.

slot  a  ovh-staging
slot  b  ovh-devops-001

timer  runner-health.yml   a  00
timer  runner-health.yml   b  30
timer  queue-watchdog.yml  a  00/20
timer  queue-watchdog.yml  b  10/20
